WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.184
- I'm actually, like
really straining, here.

00:00:02.184 --> 00:00:03.597
(exhales)

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:04.430
(tinfoil tears)

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.263
- [Producer] Oh!

00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:06.200
- Ah!

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.783
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.970
Hey, what's up, everyone?

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.150
My name is Tway and
welcome to "Making it Big,"

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.950
the show where my friends challenge me

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.140
to make their favorite foods... big.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.410
So, if you notice that my
table is a little warped here,

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.100
that's because we're filming
everything with a VR camera.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.150
Very fancy.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.190
If you wanna watch the full VR episode,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.340
you can with a Meta Quest 2 in Mega Tasty.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.900
That's our virtual cooking world

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.080
within Horizon World or on Meta Quest TV.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.800
So today, I have my favorite person here.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.072
Soybean!

00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:44.035
(both screaming in joy)

00:00:44.035 --> 00:00:47.190
Hi! Welcome to the kitchen!

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.070
- Excited to be here,
excited to challenge you.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.420
- Let's see what it is.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.704
- To match my outfit, today...

00:00:52.704 --> 00:00:55.037
(drum roll)

00:00:55.962 --> 00:00:57.690
Takis!

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.520
- Did you know that
these were my favorite?

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.380
- Maybe a hint or two, but also,

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.550
they're one of my favorite chips.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.840
- How big do you want this?

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.260
- So knowing you, usually you
like to take the challenge

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.580
and up it even more, right?

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.290
Big personality, big everything.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.480
But I want you to try to make
this like a baseball bat.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.490
I wanna be able to get
a big swing out of it.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.500
- So, big as a baseball bat.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.592
Fuego, flavor.

00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:18.480
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.640
- How important is the crunch for you?

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.630
- Super important.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.030
That crunch factor needs to be, oof!

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.950
'Cuz that's, that's the most
important part of Takis, right?

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.600
Like you hear people... (chomping)

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.350
- Yeah. All right, thanks but
I have a lot of work to do.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.882
I will see you later,
hopefully, with giant Takis.

00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:35.070
- I have faith in you (whispers).

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:35.903
Good job, buddy.

00:01:35.903 --> 00:01:36.736
- Thank you.

00:01:36.736 --> 00:01:37.569
- Good luck.

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:41.791
- Okay guys, let's make this big.

00:01:41.791 --> 00:01:42.624
(whooshing)

00:01:42.624 --> 00:01:44.280
All right, giant Takis.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.070
So, that means giant tortilla.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.150
Now, I'm kind of nervous

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:53.150
because I have never made a
tortilla from scratch before.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.600
So, to make a big one is kind of scary.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.550
I have salt, right here.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.220
I have some vegetable oil, here.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.600
So I'm using hot water

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.600
because it slows the gluten formation.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.880
It makes the tortilla not puff up.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.860
Like, we don't want this to be bread.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.080
We want this to be a tortilla.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.245
It smells like tamales, right now.

00:02:15.245 --> 00:02:17.850
(sniffing)

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.900
So, when I moved from Vietnam to America,

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:25.380
we moved to a town called Oxnard.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.480
It was a culture shock that I

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.210
didn't know I was going to experience.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.300
Like, I didn't really experience
white culture like that

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.590
but I did experience a lot

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:38.460
of Mexican culture because all
of my friends were Mexican.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.870
So, for my first ever
Christmas, I didn't know that,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.270
like tamales was a thing on Christmas.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.300
And now, every year on
Christmas, I have to have tamales

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.700
because it's just not the same without it.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.850
Okay, that feels pretty good to me.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.120
I'm gonna... Ooh!

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.180
(batter smacking)

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.803
Let's get my hands in here.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.417
I think we are ready for an ASMR moment.

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:04.739
(Batter smacking)

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:07.322
(upbeat music)

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.410
Okay, so this is the Takis fuego flavor

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.510
and I'm looking at the back

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:19.350
of it just to find what
I need for the seasoning.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:23.010
I think I'm ready to rock and roll.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.410
Let's do our habanero, right here.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.410
Cayenne pepper, garlic powder,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.850
onion powder, paprika, chili powder.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.920
Add some sugar, in here.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.610
I'm really hoping that
all of these powders

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:43.560
and spices will make my
Takis taste like Takis

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.630
because that's important.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:49.350
I need to, I really
need to deliver for Soy.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.960
The citric acid. (whispers)

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.360
And again, the reason why
I'm adding this coloring is

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:58.620
because I know that if
I don't, the color's not

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.000
going to be vibrant enough and...

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.453
Oh, it's getting me. (strained voice)

00:04:05.453 --> 00:04:06.680
Now, hold.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.259
(plastic crinkling) (coughing)

00:04:08.259 --> 00:04:10.627
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:04:10.627 --> 00:04:11.460
- (exhales)

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.570
All right, let's get back to work.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.630
It needs to look exactly like the Takis

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.480
that you see when you open up the bag.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.740
Ooh, this is probably the
most satisfying moment

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.359
for me, to seeing all of the colors.

00:04:26.359 --> 00:04:27.192
(coughs)

00:04:27.192 --> 00:04:28.070
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.670
- Just gonna... (smacking lips)

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.700
Ooh, that tastes like a Taki!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.700
All I gotta do now is grind
it up into a finer powder.

00:04:41.112 --> 00:04:41.945
(coughs)

00:04:41.945 --> 00:04:43.680
Okay.
- [Producer] Fuego! Fuego!

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.069
- I'm going through it. (strained voice)

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:45.997
(coughs)
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:04:45.997 --> 00:04:46.830
- Oh...

00:04:48.876 --> 00:04:49.709
(sneezing)

00:04:49.709 --> 00:04:50.592
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:04:50.592 --> 00:04:53.079
(Tway laughing)

00:04:53.079 --> 00:04:55.380
- If you ever attempt
to make Takis at home,

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.013
make sure that you have a mask.

00:05:00.364 --> 00:05:02.010
(food processor humming)

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.212
Huh?

00:05:03.212 --> 00:05:07.260
So, it just doesn't look a like

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:12.260
it's getting to the fine
powder, that I'm looking for.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:17.850
Because this coating right
here, is really, really fine.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.716
And it's, it's just not
what I'm looking for.

00:05:20.716 --> 00:05:22.572
(food processor container clicking)

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:23.490
(exhales loudly)

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.600
I have something...

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.140
The world's smallest spice grinder.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.807
(playful music)

00:05:33.751 --> 00:05:37.251
(spice grinder whirring)

00:05:38.817 --> 00:05:40.170
All right.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:44.460
This is definitely what I'm looking for.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:47.521
Yeah, that's good stuff!

00:05:47.521 --> 00:05:50.104
(upbeat music)

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:56.490
Okay. My dough has been
rested, and I did the math.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.530
This dough right here, will make

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:02.073
approximately six giant Takis.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.217
Perfect!

00:06:05.217 --> 00:06:08.384
(wax paper crinkling)

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.516
It looks like Patrick
Star, right now. (chuckles)

00:06:17.516 --> 00:06:19.170
(wax paper crinkles)

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.750
The middle's kind of...

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.320
Well, this is not an oval
that I'm hoping for, but

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.920
since we're going to be rolling
it, I kind of don't mind it.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.960
It's also my first one.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.490
All right.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.080
This is super delicate.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.080
Be really slow and gentle with it.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.333
I think this is the hardest step.

00:06:40.562 --> 00:06:41.760
Ooh!

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.560
This is my first giant
Takis, that's gonna go

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.785
into the oven at 350 for an hour.

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:53.368
(upbeat music)

00:06:55.770 --> 00:07:00.770
All right, so this is our big giant Takis.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.190
Can you guys see me?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:05.970
This is cooked all the way
through, but it's not crispy.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:09.036
I need it to really crisp
and have that crunch,

00:07:09.036 --> 00:07:11.286
(chomping)

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.160
when we bite into it.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.823
So, to the fryer, I go.

00:07:16.823 --> 00:07:19.406
(upbeat music)

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.540
Here we go!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.873
(drum roll)

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.490
Okay. That was really peaceful.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.990
Thank you for that.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.089
The color looks incredible.

00:07:33.089 --> 00:07:34.710
(Taki crackling)

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.210
- [Crowd] Ooh...!

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.356
Here you go.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.939
(upbeat music)

00:07:42.519 --> 00:07:44.610
(hollow tapping)

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.043
Yep, that feels crunchy.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:48.743
Here we go!

00:07:49.686 --> 00:07:54.410
So, I really want to pack in the powder.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.350
Are you serious?!

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.940
Look at this!

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.710
It's kind of taking everything

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.080
in me right now, to not take a bite.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.290
Let's, let's call Soy and
have her come in sooner,

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.050
rather than later, because
this might not be here later.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.633
(upbeat music)

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:18.960
Super proud of what we've created.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.750
I just really hope that Soy loves it.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.250
Soybean!

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.600
- Tway, should I opened my eyes?

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.100
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.000
Okay, come here.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.950
- I wanted the surprise factor, you know?

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:29.783
- Yeah.

00:08:29.783 --> 00:08:30.616
Okay, ready?

00:08:30.616 --> 00:08:32.586
- Yeah.
- 3, 2, 1.

00:08:32.586 --> 00:08:34.440
(exciting music)

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.901
- You got the bag, too?

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:36.870
- Yeah!

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.310
- That's crazy!

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:39.690
- Shout out to our department.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.310
Do you want to hold one?

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.480
- I would love to hold...

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:43.890
Yeah, as many as I can.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.703
Huh! (laughs)

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.536
- I'm gonna get one from me, too.

00:08:49.536 --> 00:08:50.369
(flute playing)

00:08:50.369 --> 00:08:51.202
A little flute.

00:08:51.202 --> 00:08:53.010
So, size?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.210
Did I pass?

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.043
- A hundred percent.

00:08:55.043 --> 00:08:56.474
Like I feel like I can...

00:08:56.474 --> 00:08:58.710
- The looks of it?

00:08:58.710 --> 00:08:59.640
- It's like, perfect.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.570
I feel like an ant.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.190
Like, you know when you
see like a giant Taki,

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.023
that's what I feel like.

00:09:03.023 --> 00:09:03.856
- Yeah.

00:09:03.856 --> 00:09:05.497
- That's amazing!

00:09:05.497 --> 00:09:07.830
(crunching)

00:09:09.389 --> 00:09:10.950
- That crunch!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.180
- That flavor!

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.070
- Oh, that is spicy.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.240
- Yeah. I can feel the heat, now.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.470
- [Producer] Fuego!

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.330
- The flavor tastes
exactly like the Takis.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.237
Like, I don't know how you did it.

00:09:20.237 --> 00:09:21.907
(crunching)

00:09:21.907 --> 00:09:23.630
(upbeat music)

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.891
(crunching)

00:09:25.891 --> 00:09:29.058
(light saber buzzing)

00:09:30.404 --> 00:09:32.249
(Soy laughing)

00:09:32.249 --> 00:09:33.600
[Soy] Wow! Saving this for later.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.250
Like, look how red our hands are.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.283
- [Tway] This is like, the best, Hmm.

00:09:37.283 --> 00:09:39.603
(static)

00:09:39.603 --> 00:09:41.741
(door creaking)

00:09:41.741 --> 00:09:44.658
(cricket chirping)

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:47.576
(foot steps tapping)

00:09:47.576 --> 00:09:50.243
(bag crinkling)

00:09:53.482 --> 00:09:56.065
(upbeat music)

